    "q-65968": {
      "dom_id": "step-q65968",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Consider the equation $\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=-\\frac{1}{2}$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$ If the solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ and ${x}_{4}$ are written in ascending order,  what is the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{3}?$",
      "worked_solution": "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & ={120}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}, & \\, & \\, & 2x & ={240}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving our two equations for $x$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{120}^{∘}}{2}+\\frac{n\\cdot {360}^{∘}}{2} & \\, & \\, & x & =\\frac{{240}^{∘}}{2}+\\frac{n\\cdot {360}^{∘}}{2} \\\\ x & ={60}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} & \\, & \\, & x & ={120}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x={60}^{∘}$ and $x={120}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x={240}^{∘}$ and $x={300}^{∘}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$ So, the solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ and ${x}_{4}$ (written in ascending order) are\n\n$$\nx={60}^{∘},\\,{120}^{∘},\\,{240}^{∘},\\,{300}^{∘}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${x}_{1}={60}^{∘}$ and ${x}_{3}={240}^{∘},$ the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{3}$ is $60\\cdot 240=14\\,400.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
