    "q-335497": {
      "dom_id": "step-q335497",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Expressed in **ascending order** in degrees, the exact solutions to the equation $3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3x}{2}-{60}^{∘})+\\frac{3}{2}=0,$ for $0\\le x<{360}^{∘},$  are\n\n${x}_{1}=$\n {{field-1}}${}^{∘},\\,{x}_{2}=$ \n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3x}{2}-{60}^{∘})+\\frac{3}{2} & =0 \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3x}{2}-{60}^{∘}) & =-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3x}{2}-{60}^{∘}) & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x}{2}-{60}^{∘} & ={120}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}, & \\, & \\, & \\frac{3x}{2}-{60}^{∘} & ={240}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x}{2} & ={120}^{∘}+{60}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘} & \\, & \\, & \\frac{3x}{2} & ={240}^{∘}+{60}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘} \\\\ \\frac{3x}{2} & ={180}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘} & \\, & \\, & \\frac{3x}{2} & ={300}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘} \\\\ 3x & ={360}^{∘}+n\\cdot {720}^{∘} & \\, & \\, & 3x & ={600}^{∘}+n\\cdot {720}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={120}^{∘}+n\\cdot {240}^{∘} & \\, & \\, & x & ={200}^{∘}+n\\cdot {240}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain\n$0\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x={120}^{∘},$ and $x={200}^{∘}.$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $0\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the solutions are\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}={120}^{∘},\\,{x}_{2}={200}^{∘}.\n$$",
