    "q-335765": {
      "dom_id": "step-q335765",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Expressed in **ascending order** in degrees, the exact solutions to the equation $4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+{30}^{∘})-2=0,$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘},$ are ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3},{x}_{4},{x}_{5},$ and ${x}_{6}.$ Determine ${x}_{2},$ ${x}_{4},$ and ${x}_{6}.$\n\n$\\,{x}_{2}=$ \n{{field-1}}${}^{∘},\\,{x}_{4}=$ \n{{field-2}}${}^{∘},\\,{x}_{6}=$ \n{{field-3}}${}^{∘}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+{30}^{∘})-2 & =0 \\\\ 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+{30}^{∘}) & =2 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x+{30}^{∘}) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+{30}^{∘} & ={60}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}, & \\, & \\, & 3x+{30}^{∘} & ={300}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x & ={60}^{∘}-{30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘} & \\, & \\, & 3x & ={300}^{∘}-{30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘} \\\\ 3x & ={30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘} & \\, & \\, & 3x & ={270}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={10}^{∘}+n\\cdot {120}^{∘} & \\, & \\, & x & ={90}^{∘}+n\\cdot {120}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x={10}^{∘}$ and $x={90}^{∘}.$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x={130}^{∘}$ and $x={210}^{∘}.$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x={250}^{∘}$ and $x={330}^{∘}.$\n\nAll other integer values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$  \n\nSo, in ascending order, the solutions are\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}={10}^{∘},\\,{x}_{2}={90}^{∘},\\,{x}_{3}={130}^{∘},\\,{x}_{4}={210}^{∘},\\,{x}_{5}={250}^{∘},\\,{x}_{6}={330}^{∘}.\n$$",
