    "q-8471": {
      "dom_id": "step-q8471",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Consider the equation $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-\\frac{7\\pi }{6})=-\\frac{1}{2}$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ If the solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ and ${x}_{4}$ are written in ascending order, what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{4}?$",
      "worked_solution": "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-\\frac{7\\pi }{6} & =-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi , & \\, & \\, & 2x-\\frac{7\\pi }{6} & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi  & \\, & \\, & 2x & =\\frac{11\\pi }{6}+2n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi  & \\, & \\, & x & =\\frac{11\\pi }{12}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{(4n+1)\\pi }{4} & \\, & \\, & x & =\\frac{(12n+11)\\pi }{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and $x=\\frac{11\\pi }{12}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{4}$ and $x=\\frac{23\\pi }{12}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$  So, the solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3},{x}_{4}$ (written in ascending order) are\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,\\frac{11\\pi }{12},\\,\\frac{5\\pi }{4},\\,\\frac{23\\pi }{12}.\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{4}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\cdot \\frac{23\\pi }{12}=\\frac{23{\\pi }^{2}}{48}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
