    "q-65971": {
      "dom_id": "step-q65971",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=\\frac{1}{2}$ for $0\\le x<\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$",
      "worked_solution": "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi , & \\, & \\, & 2x & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi  & \\, & \\, & 2x & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi  \\\\ x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi  & \\, & \\, & x & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{(6n-1)\\pi }{6} & \\, & \\, & x & =\\frac{(6n+1)\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $0\\le x<\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$ We reject the solution $-\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ since it lies outside the domain of interest.\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}$ and $x=\\frac{7\\pi }{6}.$ We reject the solution $\\frac{7\\pi }{6}$ since it lies outside the domain of interest.\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $0\\le x<\\pi .$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\cdot \\frac{5\\pi }{6}=\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{36}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
